# Typecheck after edits

CI always runs `npm run tsc --workspaces` (`tsc -p ./tsconfig.json --noEmit` per package). Package `tsconfig.json` includes `test/`, so a test-only error fails the job even when `npm test` is green.

## When finishing a change

1. Run `npm run tsc` in each package you edited (`cd packages/tx && npm run tsc`). If several packages changed, `npm run tsc --workspaces` from the repo root (same as CI).
2. Fix the errors. A mixed-type loop (e.g. the tx matrix) does not narrow: guard with `'accessList' in tx` or similar before reading a field that only some types have. Spreading a class instance into a union of `create*` factories needs a cast or a typed `txData` object — do not leave that for CI.
3. Do not leave typecheck failures for CI to catch.

`npm test` does not run `tsc`.
